---
title: "Dialog"
description: "Modal dialog built on the native dialog element."
tags: [overlay, accessibility, javascript]
usage: |
  Add the `dialog` class to a `<dialog>`, and give the button that opens it
  `data-dialog-open` with the dialog's id. Then call `initDialogs()`:

  ```js
  import { initDialogs } from "./dialog.js";

  initDialogs(); // or initDialogs(root, "[data-dialog-open]")
  ```

  A `<form method="dialog">` inside closes the dialog when submitted; the
  submitting button's `value` becomes `dialog.returnValue`.
accessibility: |
  - `showModal()` traps focus in the dialog, makes the rest of the page inert and
    closes on Escape. Focus returns to the opening button when it closes.
  - Label the dialog with `aria-labelledby` pointing at its heading.
  - Put `autofocus` on the control that should receive focus first, usually the
    least destructive action.
customProperties:
  "--dialog-border": "Border around the dialog."
  "--dialog-radius": "Corner radius."
  "--dialog-padding": "Inner spacing."
  "--dialog-max-inline-size": "Maximum width."
  "--dialog-backdrop": "Color of the backdrop behind the dialog."
  "--dialog-actions-gap": "Space between the action buttons."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<button type="button" data-dialog-open="example-dialog">Open dialog</button>

<dialog id="example-dialog" class="dialog" aria-labelledby="example-dialog-title">
  <form method="dialog">
    <h3 id="example-dialog-title">Dialog title</h3>
    <p>Dialog content goes here.</p>
    <menu>
      <button value="cancel">Cancel</button>
      <button value="confirm" autofocus>Confirm</button>
    </menu>
  </form>
</dialog>

<script type="module">
  import { initDialogs } from "./dialog.js";

  initDialogs();
</script>
